# The audio, which is everything this pack exists to carry.
#
# Not committing it is a decision that has not been taken yet, not one that has
# been taken against it. The corpus is around seven gigabytes across twelve
# packs; whether that belongs in git history, in a release asset, or somewhere
# else entirely is the owner's call and it is still open. Ignoring it for now
# leaves both doors open -- nothing is in history that a later change of mind
# would have to be rewritten to undo, and lifting the rule is deleting one line.
#
# The consequence, while the rule stands: a checkout of this repository is not
# installable. Tools/build_pack.py in the engine repository assembles the
# playable pack out of these files plus the clips.
/sounds/

/release/
/curseforge/
*.zip
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
